.TH PSVectorEquals 3 2024-03-09 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSVectorEquals\fR \- Compare two vectors

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSVectorEquals\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIPSFloat *b\fR, \fIlong length\fR, \fIint precision\fR, \fIlong *index\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare two vectors \fIa\fR and \fIb\fR having \fIlength\fR length. Use \fIprecision\fR to set precision tolerance. Lower precision leads to higher tolerance.
.br
By setting \fIprecision\fR to zero, the two vectors must be perfectly equal (no precision tolerance at all).
.br
Use \fIindex\fR pointer if you need to know the index of the first non-equal elements.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 if \fIa\fR and \fIb\fR equal, 0 if they differ at some point.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
